{
  "description": "A v4 `eachValue` rule on an object and on an array, with rules defined below its values (`$.chips.*.amount`, `$.items[*].amount`, at the root, merged with a rule for the items, and for one key). pact_verifier_cli 1.3.5 matches the values by the `eachValue` rule's own rules only, so it passes every reply here; pact-reference#586 fixes that, and a verifier with the fix fails the replies with a decimal amount. A tripwire: when the pin moves to that verifier, these interactions become disagreements, and the legacy compiler is changed to match (rholshausen/pact-janus#16, which lists what changes; ADR 0042 records today's behaviour)",
  "source": "pact-foundation/pact-reference#586; its default-engine fix, pact-reference 1f1c2e61, 2e47687e and 17aa4910, and the V2 engine's, e441f98c",
  "pacts": [
    "pact.json"
  ],
  "provider": {
    "kind": "scripted",
    "state-callback": "none",
    "routes": [
      {
        "request": {
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/chips"
        },
        "response": {
          "status": 200,
          "headers": {
            "Content-Type": [
              "application/json"
            ]
          },
          "body": {
            "json": {
              "chips": {
                "main": {
                  "amount": 500
                },
                "pair": {
                  "amount": 100
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
